{
  "_note": "Appendix-C R4 engineering-metadata model (DRAFT \u2014 appendix-c-feedback). The SMALL curated attribute set that helps a reader organize the catalogue without bloating the equal-sized brick (R4 warns against overload; R6 keeps bricks equal-weight). CHIP LINE (shown on every brick, replacing the earlier `zone \u00b7 family \u00b7 Soft/Hard` line): Family \u00b7 Primary-concern \u00b7 Enforcement \u00b7 Applicability. Role/zone is NOT a chip \u2014 it is carried by the C.1/C.2/C.3 section the brick sits in, so repeating it per brick is redundant. HELD (curated for the online catalogue only, not shown on the print brick): Primary-substrate (Git/Model/Runtime/Artifact/Prompt) and Execution-point (GitHook/ClaudeHook/CI/Runtime/Deployment) \u2014 valuable but they add two more chips and correlate with Enforcement+concern; the online full-doc surface (R1) is their home. DERIVED fields (role, enforcement, flagship, B-note locator) are computed at build time, NOT stored here. Only the CURATED judgment field (primary_concern) plus the applicability cross-reference live in this file, per the declared->derived idiom. Vocabulary uses 'structured', not 'typed'.",
  "_chip_line": {
    "shown": [
      "family (derived from path)",
      "primary_concern (curated, this file)",
      "enforcement (derived from card Enf. row)",
      "applicability (curated, applicability-DRAFT.json)"
    ],
    "not_a_chip": [
      "role/zone \u2014 carried by the C.1/C.2/C.3 section header"
    ],
    "held_for_online_only": [
      "primary_substrate",
      "execution_point"
    ],
    "example": "Context-and-dispatch \u00b7 Admission \u00b7 Hard \u00b7 Essential"
  },
  "_primary_concern_vocabulary": {
    "_kind": "closed, reader-facing set of 9 concerns; each cross-walks 1:1 to a GEE capability in catalogue-classification.json (the repo's own concern taxonomy) so the chip adopts an existing schema rather than inventing one; per-entry assignment is CURATED judgment, not the parent L2 capability copied verbatim",
    "concerns": {
      "Context": {
        "gloss": "deliver the right rules and knowledge to the actor at the point of action",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-CONSTRAIN"
      },
      "Admission": {
        "gloss": "gate the work order and the path to production",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-ADMIT"
      },
      "Orchestration": {
        "gloss": "manage fleet work, state, resources, and lifecycle",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-MANAGE"
      },
      "Modeling": {
        "gloss": "represent the system as authoritative structured models the fleet reasons through",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-KNOW"
      },
      "Synchronization": {
        "gloss": "keep the models equal to the code and system they describe",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-SYNC"
      },
      "Validation": {
        "gloss": "check output conforms and establish completion on re-derived evidence",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-COMPLETE"
      },
      "Provenance": {
        "gloss": "durably attribute every mutation and trace its cause",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-PROVENANCE"
      },
      "Governance": {
        "gloss": "govern the control estate itself",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-GOVERN"
      },
      "Constraint": {
        "gloss": "confine mutation to sanctioned surfaces and closed action vocabularies",
        "gee_capability": "CAP-CONSTRAIN"
      }
    }
  },
